  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $A$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $A$ where every element of $A$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nTo find the subset that goes in the blank, we must identify which elements of $A$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets.\n\nLet's go through each element of $X$ and check:\n\n- $-3\\in {-3,-2,-1}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $-2\\in {-3,-2,-1}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $-3\\in {-3,-2,-1}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $0$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $1\\in {1,2,3}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $2\\in {1,2,3}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $3\\in {1,2,3}\\,\u2713$\n\nThe element  $0$ is not yet contained within any of the given subsets. Therefore, the subset that must go in the blank is ${0}.$",
